{
  "id": "continuous-reinforcement",
  "term": "continuous reinforcement",
  "definition": "Continuous reinforcement is a learning schedule in which a behavior is rewarded every time it occurs, creating a complete link between the response and the reinforcer. It is contrasted with partial reinforcement, where rewards are given only some of the time.",
